From c46cb02264c3e5e24baf6ab0946fc10b728a6d34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Reategui Solis <reateguisolisjm@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:57:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bionic: raise() signals the calling thread with tgkill
 directly

raise() went through pthread_kill(), which takes gThreadListLock. When
dlmalloc detects heap corruption it calls abort() with the malloc lock
held; if another thread holds gThreadListLock while waiting for malloc
(thread exit/creation), the process deadlocks instead of dying.

On g2mv this left mediaserver wedged after "heap corruption detected by
dlfree": every audio binder call (Ringer, ToneGenerator, InCallUI) hung,
so incoming calls never showed. Matches the upstream Lollipop raise().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ie7bbccdf26dc41f5156ddf7e4fef1cbe74c53b90
---
 libc/bionic/raise.cpp | 17 ++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libc/bionic/raise.cpp b/libc/bionic/raise.cpp
index f69d90b60..aec683943 100644
--- a/libc/bionic/raise.cpp
+++ b/libc/bionic/raise.cpp
@@ -26,13 +26,16 @@
  * SUCH DAMAGE.
  */
 
-#include <pthread.h>
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <signal.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 
+extern "C" int tgkill(int tgid, int tid, int sig);
+
+// Signal the calling thread directly. Going through pthread_kill() takes
+// gThreadListLock; if abort() is called from inside dlmalloc (heap
+// corruption) while another thread holds that lock and waits for the
+// malloc lock, the process deadlocks instead of dying. (Upstream L fix.)
 int raise(int sig) {
-  int rc = pthread_kill(pthread_self(), sig);
-  if (rc != 0) {
-    errno = rc;
-    return -1;
-  }
-  return 0;
+  return tgkill(getpid(), gettid(), sig);
 }
